WEBVTT

00:00:05.803 --> 00:00:07.310
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:07.316 --> 00:00:08.885
Let's say good night to your brother.

00:00:09.088 --> 00:00:10.148
Night, Sam.

00:00:10.272 --> 00:00:11.652
Hey, Dean.

00:00:11.677 --> 00:00:13.206
Daddy! Hey, buddy.

00:00:14.127 --> 00:00:15.734
Sweet dreams, Sam.

00:00:19.892 --> 00:00:22.370
Dad's missing. I need
you to help me find him.

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:24.317
The trail for dad, it's getting colder.

00:00:24.441 --> 00:00:27.031
Every day. You don't think I want
to find dad as much as you do?

00:00:27.055 --> 00:00:28.433
I know you do. Find dad.

00:00:28.457 --> 00:00:30.750
Mom's gone. She isn't coming back.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:35.151
Don't talk about her like that.

00:00:58.344 --> 00:00:59.599
Mommy?

00:01:01.259 --> 00:01:03.188
Hey, sweetie.

00:01:03.464 --> 00:01:07.413
Why aren't you in bed?
There's something in my closet.

00:01:23.231 --> 00:01:24.071
See?

00:01:24.106 --> 00:01:25.385
There's nothing there.

00:01:26.763 --> 00:01:29.702
You're sure? I'm sure.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:37.990
Now, come on.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.101
Into bed.

00:01:46.544 --> 00:01:48.167
I don't like this house.

00:01:48.782 --> 00:01:50.381
You're just not used to it yet.

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:57.045
But you and your brother and me,
we are going to be very happy here.

00:01:57.596 --> 00:01:58.604
I promise.

00:02:01.209 --> 00:02:02.864
I love you.

00:02:10.664 --> 00:02:11.417
The chair.

00:02:12.299 --> 00:02:13.712
Okay.

00:02:14.351 --> 00:02:15.329
Right.

00:02:19.204 --> 00:02:20.258
The chair.

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:24.572
Just to be safe.

00:02:56.812 --> 00:03:00.348
Please, god, don't let it be rats.

00:03:20.057 --> 00:03:21.294
Terrific.

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:19.578
All right.

00:05:19.603 --> 00:05:21.400
I've been cruising some websites.

00:05:21.505 --> 00:05:23.899
Think I found a few
candidates for our next gig.

00:05:25.206 --> 00:05:27.963
A fishing trawler found
off the coast of Cali.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.486
Its crew vanished.

00:05:29.717 --> 00:05:33.200
And we got some cattle
mutilations in west Texas.

00:05:33.682 --> 00:05:34.299
Hey!

00:05:36.131 --> 00:05:38.193
Am I boring you with
this hunting-Evil stuff?

00:05:38.733 --> 00:05:40.815
No, I'm listening. Keep going.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:45.596
And here a Sacramento man
shot himself in the head...

00:05:46.039 --> 00:05:47.273
Three times.

00:05:49.711 --> 00:05:51.754
Any of these things
blowing up your skirt, pal?

00:05:55.783 --> 00:05:57.817
Wait, I've seen this. Seen what?

00:06:04.678 --> 00:06:05.791
What are you doing?

00:06:14.132 --> 00:06:15.872
Dean, I know where we have to go next.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:16.584
Where?

00:06:17.213 --> 00:06:18.151
Back home.

00:06:18.965 --> 00:06:19.989
Back to Kansas.

00:06:21.383 --> 00:06:23.258
Okay, random. Where'd that come from?

00:06:24.140 --> 00:06:25.152
All right, um...

00:06:25.192 --> 00:06:27.521
This photo was taken in
front of our old house, right?

00:06:27.606 --> 00:06:28.821
The house where mom died?

00:06:30.266 --> 00:06:30.922
Yeah.

00:06:30.999 --> 00:06:34.161
It didn't burn down right? I mean not
completely, they rebuilt it, right?

00:06:34.238 --> 00:06:36.590
I guess so, yeah. What the
hell are you talking about?

00:06:36.621 --> 00:06:38.831
Okay, look, this is gonna sound crazy,

00:06:38.861 --> 00:06:40.944
But the people who
live in our old house,

00:06:42.212 --> 00:06:43.851
I think they might be in danger.

00:06:44.196 --> 00:06:46.566
Why would you think that? Uh...

00:06:46.624 --> 00:06:48.646
Just, um... look, just...

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.030
You got to trust me on this, okay?

00:06:51.667 --> 00:06:53.736
Hey, whoa, whoa, whoa. Trust you? Yeah.

00:06:54.254 --> 00:06:56.158
You got to give me a
little bit more than that.

00:06:56.204 --> 00:06:57.936
I can't really explain, it is all.

00:06:58.141 --> 00:07:00.665
Well, tough. I'm not going
anywhere until you do.

00:07:05.327 --> 00:07:07.023
I have these nightmares.

00:07:07.324 --> 00:07:08.728
I've noticed.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:13.514
And sometimes they come true.

00:07:16.566 --> 00:07:17.574
Come again?

00:07:18.437 --> 00:07:19.116
Look, Dean...

00:07:20.309 --> 00:07:21.773
I dreamt about Jessica's death

00:07:22.572 --> 00:07:24.484
For days before it happened.

00:07:27.083 --> 00:07:29.827
Sane people have weird dreams, man.
I'm sure it's just a coincidence.

00:07:30.376 --> 00:07:33.510
No, I dreamt about the blood dripping,
her on the ceiling, the fire, everything,

00:07:33.522 --> 00:07:35.389
And I didn't do anything
'cause I didn't believe it.

00:07:35.447 --> 00:07:37.067
Now I'm dreaming about that tree,

00:07:37.236 --> 00:07:40.087
About our house, and some woman
inside screaming for help. I mean,

00:07:40.276 --> 00:07:42.716
That's where it all started, man.
This has to mean something, right?

00:07:44.991 --> 00:07:45.824
I don't know.

00:07:46.844 --> 00:07:49.025
What do you mean you
don't know, Dean? This...

00:07:49.143 --> 00:07:50.832
This woman might be in danger.

00:07:50.891 --> 00:07:55.031
This might be the thing that killed mom and
Jessica. All right, just slow down,would you?

00:07:59.066 --> 00:08:01.670
I mean, first you're telling
me that you've got this Shining

00:08:02.879 --> 00:08:04.756
and then you tell me that
I've got to go back home,

00:08:05.999 --> 00:08:06.922
Especially when...

00:08:08.905 --> 00:08:10.009
When what?

00:08:11.427 --> 00:08:13.714
When I swore to myself that
I would never go back there.

00:08:25.115 --> 00:08:27.062
Dean, we have to check this out.

00:08:28.208 --> 00:08:29.608
Just to make sure.

00:08:36.936 --> 00:08:38.027
I know we do.

00:08:56.466 --> 00:08:58.066
You gonna be all right, man?

00:08:59.967 --> 00:09:01.793
Let me get back to you on that.

00:09:09.865 --> 00:09:10.358
Yes?

00:09:10.628 --> 00:09:11.988
Sorry to bother you, ma'am,

00:09:12.099 --> 00:09:14.492
But we're with the
federal... I'm Sam Winchester

00:09:14.726 --> 00:09:16.486
And this is my brother, Dean.

00:09:16.550 --> 00:09:18.884
Um...we used to live here.

00:09:19.799 --> 00:09:22.169
You know, we were just driving by, and

00:09:22.222 --> 00:09:24.603
We were wondering if we
could come see the old place.

00:09:24.664 --> 00:09:25.825
Winchester...

00:09:27.362 --> 00:09:28.817
That is so funny.

00:09:29.013 --> 00:09:32.333
You know, I, I think I found some
of your photos the other night.

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:33.025
You did?

00:09:37.291 --> 00:09:39.441
Okay. Come on in.

00:09:51.381 --> 00:09:53.446
Juice, juice, juice!

00:09:53.481 --> 00:09:55.399
Juice, juice,  juice!

00:09:55.422 --> 00:09:59.293
That's Richie. He's
kind of a juice junkie.

00:09:59.532 --> 00:10:02.499
But, hey, at least he won't get scurvy.

00:10:03.755 --> 00:10:04.857
Sari,

00:10:05.268 --> 00:10:07.368
This is Sam and Dean.

00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:09.351
They used to live here. Hi.

00:10:09.879 --> 00:10:10.817
Hey, Sari.

00:10:11.768 --> 00:10:13.070
So, you just moved in?

00:10:13.128 --> 00:10:14.853
Uh, yeah, from Wichita.

00:10:14.955 --> 00:10:16.375
You got family here?

00:10:17.466 --> 00:10:19.436
No, I just, uh...

00:10:20.598 --> 00:10:23.759
Um, needed a fresh start. That's all.

00:10:24.888 --> 00:10:27.089
So new town,

00:10:27.199 --> 00:10:28.317
New job

00:10:28.501 --> 00:10:30.333
I mean, as soon as I find one,

00:10:30.737 --> 00:10:32.001
New house.

00:10:34.056 --> 00:10:35.816
So, how you liking it so far?

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.783
Well, uh, all due respect
to your childhood home,

00:10:40.875 --> 00:10:44.320
I mean, I'm sure you have
lots of happy memories here,

00:10:44.778 --> 00:10:47.051
But this place has its issues.

00:10:47.326 --> 00:10:48.536
What do you mean?

00:10:49.909 --> 00:10:51.706
Well, it's just getting old

00:10:52.109 --> 00:10:54.235
Like, the wiring, you know? We've got

00:10:54.363 --> 00:10:56.471
Flickering lights almost hourly.

00:10:56.581 --> 00:10:57.827
Oh, that's too bad.

00:10:58.304 --> 00:10:59.330
What else?

00:10:59.678 --> 00:11:03.986
Um...sink's backed up.
There's rats in the basement.

00:11:06.096 --> 00:11:07.526
I'm sorry.

00:11:07.691 --> 00:11:09.798
I don't mean to complain. No.

00:11:09.872 --> 00:11:13.262
Have you seen the rats or
have you just heard scratching?

00:11:14.344 --> 00:11:17.386
Just the scratching, actually. Mom?

00:11:21.784 --> 00:11:24.790
Ask them if it was here
when they lived here.

00:11:26.183 --> 00:11:27.228
What, Sari?

00:11:28.016 --> 00:11:29.739
The thing in my closet.

00:11:29.769 --> 00:11:34.056
Oh, no, baby, there was
nothing in their closets.

00:11:34.209 --> 00:11:35.011
Right?

00:11:35.836 --> 00:11:38.083
Right, no.No, of course not.

00:11:39.345 --> 00:11:41.958
She had a nightmare the other night.

00:11:42.073 --> 00:11:43.586
I wasn't dreaming.

00:11:43.770 --> 00:11:47.186
It came into my bedroom,
and it was on fire.

00:11:48.179 --> 00:11:51.114
You heard that ? A figure on fire.

00:11:51.437 --> 00:11:53.785
And that woman Jenny, that was
the woman in your dreams? Yeah.

00:11:53.857 --> 00:11:56.607
And you hear what she was talking
about ? Scratching, flickering lights ?

00:11:56.683 --> 00:11:58.907
Both signs of a malevolent
spirit. Yeah well.

00:11:59.022 --> 00:12:01.161
I'm just freaked out your
weirdo visions are coming true.

00:12:01.177 --> 00:12:02.347
Forget about that for a minute.

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:05.213
The thing in the house, do you think it's the
thing that killed mom and Jessica? I don't know!

00:12:05.439 --> 00:12:07.474
Has it come back or has it
been there the whole time?

00:12:07.479 --> 00:12:09.824
Maybe it's something else
entirely. Sam, we don't know yet.

00:12:09.833 --> 00:12:11.607
Those people are in danger, Dean.

00:12:12.023 --> 00:12:13.992
We have to get them out
of that house. And we will.

00:12:14.022 --> 00:12:15.832
No, I mean now. And how
you're gonna do that ?

00:12:15.849 --> 00:12:18.477
You got a story she's gonna believe?
Then what are we supposed to do?!

00:12:19.013 --> 00:12:20.741
We just got to chill out, that's all.

00:12:21.596 --> 00:12:23.953
If this was any other kind
of job, what would we do?

00:12:29.052 --> 00:12:30.949
We'd try to figure out
what we were dealing with.

00:12:31.503 --> 00:12:34.042
We'd dig into the history
of the house. Exactly.

00:12:34.065 --> 00:12:35.601
Except this time we
already know what happened.

00:12:35.634 --> 00:12:39.230
Yeah, but how much do we know?
How much do you actually remember?

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.118
About that night, you mean? Yeah.

00:12:45.063 --> 00:12:46.032
Not much.

00:12:47.484 --> 00:12:48.849
I remember the fire...

00:12:49.847 --> 00:12:50.742
The heat.

00:12:54.662 --> 00:12:56.158
Then I carried you out the front door.

00:12:58.902 --> 00:12:59.739
You did?

00:13:01.559 --> 00:13:02.982
Yeah, well, you never knew that?

00:13:05.309 --> 00:13:06.150
No.

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:09.088
And, uh...

00:13:09.161 --> 00:13:11.641
Well, you know dad's story
as well as I do. Mom was...

00:13:13.182 --> 00:13:14.253
Was on the ceiling.

00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:17.555
Whatever put her there was long
gone by the time dad found her.

00:13:18.583 --> 00:13:21.277
And he never had a
theory about what did it?

00:13:21.782 --> 00:13:23.353
If he did, he kept it to himself.

00:13:24.264 --> 00:13:26.538
God knows we asked him enough times.

00:13:29.488 --> 00:13:30.324
Okay.

00:13:31.235 --> 00:13:33.744
So, if we're gonna figure
out what's going on now,

00:13:35.109 --> 00:13:36.914
We have to figure out
what happened back then,

00:13:38.191 --> 00:13:39.790
And see if it's the same thing.

00:13:39.952 --> 00:13:40.421
Yeah.

00:13:41.815 --> 00:13:44.904
Talk to dad's friends, neighbors,
people who were there at the time.

00:13:46.824 --> 00:13:49.125
Does this feel like
just another job to you?

00:13:55.824 --> 00:13:57.599
I'll be right back. I
got to go to the bathroom.

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:17.922
<i>This is John Winchester.</i>

00:14:17.994 --> 00:14:24.289
<i>If this is an emergency, call
my son Dean, 866 907 32 35.</i>

00:14:24.333 --> 00:14:24.847
Dad...

00:14:28.062 --> 00:14:30.515
I know I've left you messages before.

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.442
I don't even know if you get 'em.

00:14:36.441 --> 00:14:36.999
But

00:14:37.469 --> 00:14:38.584
I'm with Sam

00:14:39.626 --> 00:14:41.167
And we're in Lawrence,

00:14:42.179 --> 00:14:44.607
And there's something in our old house.

00:14:45.936 --> 00:14:48.688
I don't know if it's the
thing that killed mom or not,

00:14:50.151 --> 00:14:50.576
But...

00:14:53.100 --> 00:14:54.982
I don't know what to do.

00:14:56.901 --> 00:14:57.679
So,

00:14:58.031 --> 00:15:00.293
Whatever you're doing,
if you could get here...

00:15:02.257 --> 00:15:03.123
Please.

00:15:05.751 --> 00:15:07.204
I need your help, dad.

00:15:12.282 --> 00:15:15.862
No, sir, nothing weird
down there. I promise.

00:15:16.361 --> 00:15:19.311
Sink just backed upon
its own. I'll take a look.

00:15:19.502 --> 00:15:20.426
Thanks.

00:15:21.556 --> 00:15:23.699
Oh, okay, I'll get out of your way.

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:09.743
So you and John Winchester, you
used to own this garage together?

00:17:09.816 --> 00:17:12.502
Yeah, we used to. A long time ago.

00:17:12.615 --> 00:17:13.495
Matter of fact,

00:17:13.715 --> 00:17:16.665
Must be 20 years since John disappeared.

00:17:16.809 --> 00:17:18.593
So, why are the cops
interested all of a sudden?

00:17:18.668 --> 00:17:22.660
Oh, we're reopening some of our unsolved cases,
and the Winchester disappearance is one of them.

00:17:22.754 --> 00:17:25.358
Uh-Huh. Well, what do you
want to know about John?

00:17:25.452 --> 00:17:27.692
Whatever you remember, you know.
Whatever sticks out in your mind.

00:17:31.228 --> 00:17:33.888
He was a stubborn
bastard. I remember that.

00:17:34.862 --> 00:17:36.059
And, uh...

00:17:36.117 --> 00:17:39.015
Oh, whatever the game, he
hated to lose, you know?

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:40.786
It was that whole marine thing.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:42.792
But, uh...

00:17:43.093 --> 00:17:44.536
Well, he sure loved Mary,

00:17:45.545 --> 00:17:47.034
And he doted on those kids.

00:17:47.515 --> 00:17:48.993
But that was before the fire.

00:17:50.081 --> 00:17:50.727
That's right.

00:17:51.043 --> 00:17:52.427
He ever talk about that night?

00:17:54.011 --> 00:17:54.606
No,

00:17:54.981 --> 00:17:56.025
Not at first.

00:17:56.717 --> 00:17:58.571
I think he was in shock. Right,

00:17:59.134 --> 00:18:00.529
But eventually,

00:18:01.597 --> 00:18:02.977
What did he say about it?

00:18:03.667 --> 00:18:06.504
Oh, he wasn't thinking
straight. He said, uh...

00:18:07.128 --> 00:18:10.613
He said something caused
that fire and killed Mary.

00:18:10.648 --> 00:18:11.678
He ever say what did it?

00:18:12.617 --> 00:18:15.136
Nothing did it. It was an accident.

00:18:15.537 --> 00:18:19.208
An electrical short in the
ceiling or walls or something.

00:18:21.156 --> 00:18:24.959
I begged him to get some
help, but... But what?

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:27.385
Oh, it just got worse and worse.

00:18:27.596 --> 00:18:28.135
How?

00:18:28.863 --> 00:18:32.382
Oh, he started reading
these strange old books.

00:18:32.417 --> 00:18:35.132
He started going to see
this palm reader in town.

00:18:35.305 --> 00:18:37.427
Palm reader? You have a name?

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:39.479
No.

00:18:43.598 --> 00:18:47.030
All right, so, there are a few
psychics and palm readers in town.

00:18:47.065 --> 00:18:49.510
There's someone named
El Divino. There's...

00:18:49.675 --> 00:18:52.443
There's the mysterious Mr. Fortinsky.

00:18:52.559 --> 00:18:55.198
Uh, Missouri Moseley,
some dude -- Wait, wait...

00:18:55.281 --> 00:18:56.407
Missouri Moseley?

00:18:56.735 --> 00:18:57.193
What?

00:18:57.509 --> 00:18:58.424
That's a psychic?

00:18:59.034 --> 00:19:01.732
Uh...yeah.Yeah, I guess so.

00:19:05.359 --> 00:19:06.263
In dad's journal...

00:19:09.653 --> 00:19:10.927
Look at this.

00:19:12.555 --> 00:19:14.957
First page, first sentence. Read that.

00:19:15.902 --> 00:19:17.228
"I went to Missouri...

00:19:18.483 --> 00:19:20.060
And I learned the truth."

00:19:20.887 --> 00:19:22.699
I always thought he meant the state.

00:19:28.511 --> 00:19:29.989
All right, then.

00:19:30.388 --> 00:19:32.347
Don't you worry about a thing.

00:19:33.156 --> 00:19:34.904
Your wife is crazy about you.

00:19:38.321 --> 00:19:40.959
Whew! Poor bastard.

00:19:41.463 --> 00:19:43.774
His woman cold-Bangin'the gardener.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:46.809
Why didn't you tell him?

00:19:47.203 --> 00:19:49.369
People don't come here for the truth.

00:19:49.404 --> 00:19:51.232
They come for good news.

00:19:52.739 --> 00:19:53.537
Well?

00:19:53.701 --> 00:19:56.960
Sam and Dean, come on
already. I ain't got all day.

00:20:05.075 --> 00:20:06.753
Well, let me look at you.

00:20:08.477 --> 00:20:11.493
Oh, you boys grew up handsome.

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:14.973
And you were one
goofy-Looking kid, too.

00:20:16.732 --> 00:20:17.765
Sam.

00:20:20.685 --> 00:20:22.163
Oh, honey.

00:20:24.052 --> 00:20:27.219
I'm sorry about your girlfriend.

00:20:27.829 --> 00:20:29.465
And your father

00:20:31.157 --> 00:20:32.681
he's missing?

00:20:35.614 --> 00:20:37.248
How'd you know all that?

00:20:37.283 --> 00:20:37.890
Well,

00:20:38.957 --> 00:20:41.840
You were just thinking it, just now.

00:20:42.361 --> 00:20:44.279
Well, where is he? Is he okay?

00:20:44.907 --> 00:20:46.318
I don't know.

00:20:46.983 --> 00:20:47.992
Don't know?

00:20:49.059 --> 00:20:50.775
You're supposed to be a psychic, right?

00:20:51.441 --> 00:20:55.542
Boy, you see me sawing
some bony tramp in half?

00:20:55.577 --> 00:20:56.974
You think I'm a magician?

00:20:57.212 --> 00:21:00.325
I may be able to read thoughts
and sense energies in a room,

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:02.548
But I can't just pull
facts out of thin air.

00:21:02.583 --> 00:21:03.021
Sit!

00:21:03.274 --> 00:21:03.904
Please.

00:21:13.994 --> 00:21:17.630
Boy, you put your foot on my coffee
table, I'm gonna whack you with a spoon.

00:21:17.665 --> 00:21:18.568
I didn't do anything.

00:21:18.653 --> 00:21:20.146
Well, you were thinking about it.

00:21:26.749 --> 00:21:28.384
Okay, so...

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:30.140
Our dad.

00:21:31.004 --> 00:21:32.461
When did you first meet him?

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.549
He came for a reading

00:21:35.245 --> 00:21:37.996
A few days after the fire.

00:21:38.884 --> 00:21:42.242
I just told him what was
really out there in the dark.

00:21:42.387 --> 00:21:44.108
I guess you could say

00:21:45.374 --> 00:21:47.467
I drew back the curtains for him.

00:21:47.493 --> 00:21:48.573
What about the fire?

00:21:49.991 --> 00:21:52.633
Do you know about what killed our mom?

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:53.734
A little.

00:21:54.674 --> 00:21:56.819
Your daddy took me to your house.

00:21:56.993 --> 00:21:58.771
He was hoping I could

00:21:58.916 --> 00:21:59.977
Sense the

00:22:00.446 --> 00:22:01.451
Echoes,

00:22:01.489 --> 00:22:03.507
The fingerprints of this thing.

00:22:03.865 --> 00:22:04.812
And could you?

00:22:05.393 --> 00:22:06.163
I don't...

00:22:07.954 --> 00:22:08.893
What was it?

00:22:09.578 --> 00:22:10.555
I don't know.

00:22:13.410 --> 00:22:15.251
But it was evil.

00:22:15.463 --> 00:22:19.858
Look, I feel just awful
about the poor man's hand,

00:22:20.851 --> 00:22:23.521
But how can I be held liable?

00:22:25.884 --> 00:22:26.467
Yeah, but

00:22:26.626 --> 00:22:28.730
I can't afford a lawyer.

00:22:31.181 --> 00:22:33.892
Okay, listen, y-You just
got to let me call you back.

00:22:35.067 --> 00:22:38.108
Richie, mommy's gonna be right back,

00:22:38.333 --> 00:22:39.075
Okay?

00:22:39.169 --> 00:22:40.014
Okay.

00:22:40.437 --> 00:22:41.064
Okay.

00:22:45.177 --> 00:22:46.135
So,

00:22:47.683 --> 00:22:50.383
You think something's
back in that house?

00:22:51.348 --> 00:22:52.877
Definitely.

00:22:56.013 --> 00:22:57.813
I don't understand.

00:22:58.386 --> 00:22:59.540
What?

00:23:02.199 --> 00:23:04.011
I haven't been back inside,

00:23:04.046 --> 00:23:08.443
But I've been keeping an eye on
the place, and it's been quiet.

00:23:08.687 --> 00:23:10.786
No sudden deaths, no

00:23:10.947 --> 00:23:12.665
Freak accidents.

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:14.288
Why is it acting up now?

00:23:14.779 --> 00:23:15.633
I don't know.

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:19.726
But dad going missing
and Jessica dying and

00:23:20.123 --> 00:23:21.677
Now this house,

00:23:22.188 --> 00:23:25.597
All happening at once. It just
feels like something's starting.

00:23:26.267 --> 00:23:28.392
That's a comforting thought.

00:23:59.438 --> 00:24:00.763
Juicy!

00:24:15.150 --> 00:24:19.031
Oh, baby, either we have
rats or mommy is going crazy.

00:24:19.745 --> 00:24:20.495
Richie?

00:24:23.229 --> 00:24:24.366
Richie?!

00:24:34.659 --> 00:24:36.997
Baby, where are you?!

00:24:45.328 --> 00:24:46.008
Wha...

00:24:54.117 --> 00:24:56.299
Mum! Oh, my god!

00:25:02.488 --> 00:25:03.661
Oh, baby!

00:25:06.724 --> 00:25:08.461
Sam, Dean,

00:25:08.836 --> 00:25:10.009
What are you doing here?

00:25:10.185 --> 00:25:11.276
Hey, Jenny.

00:25:11.546 --> 00:25:13.909
Um, this is our friend Missouri.

00:25:14.731 --> 00:25:18.068
If it's not too much trouble, we were
hoping to show her the house, you know,

00:25:18.231 --> 00:25:20.139
For old time's sake.

00:25:20.174 --> 00:25:22.428
No, you know, this isn't a good time.

00:25:22.463 --> 00:25:24.424
I'm kind of busy. Listen,
Jenny,it's important.

00:25:24.569 --> 00:25:25.058
Ow!

00:25:25.419 --> 00:25:28.738
Give the poor girl a break.
Can't you see she's upset?

00:25:28.773 --> 00:25:30.204
Forgive this boy. He means well.

00:25:30.239 --> 00:25:32.275
He's just not the
sharpest tool in the shed.

00:25:32.310 --> 00:25:33.691
But hear me out.

00:25:34.295 --> 00:25:35.401
About what?

00:25:35.459 --> 00:25:36.725
About this house.

00:25:37.520 --> 00:25:38.902
What are you talking about?

00:25:39.397 --> 00:25:42.125
I think you know what I'm talking about.

00:25:42.160 --> 00:25:47.091
You think there's something in this house,
something that wants to hurt your family.

00:25:47.126 --> 00:25:48.580
Am I mistaken?

00:25:49.514 --> 00:25:51.251
Who are you?

00:25:51.286 --> 00:25:54.554
We're people who can help,
who can stop this thing,

00:25:54.589 --> 00:25:57.042
But you're gonna have to
trust us, just a little.

00:25:59.764 --> 00:26:04.968
If there's a dark energy around here,
this room should be the center of it.

00:26:06.317 --> 00:26:07.128
Why?

00:26:07.658 --> 00:26:10.335
This used to be your nursery, Sam.

00:26:10.370 --> 00:26:12.646
This is where it all happened.

00:26:27.935 --> 00:26:29.612
That an emf?

00:26:30.006 --> 00:26:30.592
Yeah.

00:26:31.552 --> 00:26:32.399
Amateur.

00:26:42.764 --> 00:26:45.602
I don't know if you boys should
be disappointed or relieved,

00:26:45.637 --> 00:26:47.818
But this ain't the
thing that took your mom.

00:26:49.478 --> 00:26:50.906
Are you sure?

00:26:51.887 --> 00:26:53.113
How do you know?

00:26:53.119 --> 00:26:56.921
It isn't the same energy I
felt the last time I was here.

00:26:56.956 --> 00:26:58.368
It's something different.

00:26:59.353 --> 00:27:00.375
What is it?

00:27:02.004 --> 00:27:03.495
Not it...

00:27:04.253 --> 00:27:05.797
Them.

00:27:06.411 --> 00:27:09.478
There's more than one
spirit in this place.

00:27:10.634 --> 00:27:12.246
What are they doing here?

00:27:12.281 --> 00:27:15.140
They're here because of
what happened to your family.

00:27:15.734 --> 00:27:17.636
You see, all those years ago,

00:27:17.728 --> 00:27:20.268
Real evil came to you.

00:27:21.648 --> 00:27:26.242
It walked this house. That
kind of evil leaves wounds,

00:27:26.277 --> 00:27:29.050
And sometimes wounds get infected.

00:27:29.366 --> 00:27:31.098
I don't understand.

00:27:31.133 --> 00:27:34.408
This place is a magnet
for paranormal energy.

00:27:37.222 --> 00:27:39.632
It's attracted a poltergeist,

00:27:40.087 --> 00:27:41.760
A nasty one,

00:27:42.527 --> 00:27:46.288
And it won't rest until
Jenny and her babies are dead.

00:27:46.323 --> 00:27:48.552
You said there was more than one spirit.

00:27:48.641 --> 00:27:50.144
There is.

00:27:53.004 --> 00:27:56.301
I just can't quite
make out the second one.

00:28:00.361 --> 00:28:02.205
Well, one thing's for damn sure,

00:28:02.793 --> 00:28:04.630
Nobody's dying in this house,

00:28:04.665 --> 00:28:05.804
Ever again.

00:28:06.484 --> 00:28:08.835
So, whatever is here, how do we stop it?

00:28:12.249 --> 00:28:14.370
So, what is all this stuff anyway?

00:28:14.811 --> 00:28:18.250
Angelica root, van van
oil, crossroad dirt,

00:28:18.305 --> 00:28:20.241
A few other odds and ends.

00:28:20.276 --> 00:28:21.505
What are we supposed to do with it?

00:28:21.540 --> 00:28:24.712
We're gonna put them inside the walls

00:28:24.928 --> 00:28:28.160
In the north, south, east, west corners

00:28:28.195 --> 00:28:30.127
On each floor of the house.

00:28:30.162 --> 00:28:33.270
Punching holes in the drywall.
Jenny's gonna love that.

00:28:34.230 --> 00:28:35.647
She'll live.

00:28:36.715 --> 00:28:38.958
And this will destroy the spirits?

00:28:38.993 --> 00:28:40.270
It should.

00:28:40.840 --> 00:28:43.461
It should purify the house completely.

00:28:44.604 --> 00:28:46.270
We'll each take a floor,

00:28:46.633 --> 00:28:48.143
But we work fast.

00:28:48.178 --> 00:28:51.039
Once the spirits
realize what we're up to,

00:28:51.067 --> 00:28:53.198
Things are gonna get bad.

00:28:54.969 --> 00:28:55.821
Okay.

00:28:57.151 --> 00:28:58.534
Careful.

00:29:00.037 --> 00:29:03.847
Look, I -You know, I'm not sure I'm
comfortable leaving you guys here alone.

00:29:03.882 --> 00:29:06.181
Just take your kids to
the movie or something, and

00:29:06.219 --> 00:29:08.373
It'll be over by the time you get back.

00:29:09.245 --> 00:29:09.937
Okay.

00:30:06.621 --> 00:30:08.372
Aah! Uhh!

00:30:46.430 --> 00:30:47.205
Sam!

00:30:49.516 --> 00:30:50.255
Sam!

00:31:13.277 --> 00:31:14.469
Come on.

00:31:36.245 --> 00:31:38.130
Are you sure this is over?

00:31:41.299 --> 00:31:42.609
I'm sure.

00:31:43.037 --> 00:31:43.646
Why?

00:31:44.796 --> 00:31:46.483
Why do you ask?

00:31:47.338 --> 00:31:48.929
No, never mind.

00:31:50.634 --> 00:31:52.481
It's nothing, I guess.

00:31:54.517 --> 00:31:55.840
Hello?

00:31:56.417 --> 00:31:57.896
We're home.

00:32:00.933 --> 00:32:02.541
What happened?

00:32:02.645 --> 00:32:05.316
Hi. Sorry. Um, we'll...

00:32:05.351 --> 00:32:07.381
We'll pay for all of this.

00:32:08.143 --> 00:32:09.575
Don't you worry.

00:32:09.633 --> 00:32:11.698
Dean's gonna clean up this mess.

00:32:14.724 --> 00:32:16.707
Well, what are you waiting for, boy?

00:32:16.742 --> 00:32:17.510
Get the mop.

00:32:18.414 --> 00:32:19.974
And don't cuss at me.

00:32:41.504 --> 00:32:42.267
Okay.

00:33:36.226 --> 00:33:38.331
So, tell me again. What
are we still doing here?

00:33:38.366 --> 00:33:39.827
I don't know, I-I just...

00:33:40.472 --> 00:33:42.056
I still have a bad feeling.

00:33:42.642 --> 00:33:43.651
Why?

00:33:44.167 --> 00:33:47.812
Missouri did her whole zelda rubenstein thing.
The house should be clean. This should be over.

00:33:48.037 --> 00:33:50.946
Yeah, probably, but I just
want to make sure. That's all.

00:33:52.410 --> 00:33:55.466
The problem is I could be
sleeping in a bed right now.

00:33:59.837 --> 00:34:00.775
Dean!

00:34:01.256 --> 00:34:01.956
Dean!

00:34:03.915 --> 00:34:05.759
You grab the kids, I'll get Jenny.

00:34:24.418 --> 00:34:26.119
Come on! Jenny!

00:34:26.157 --> 00:34:28.775
I can't open the door! Stand back!

00:34:31.841 --> 00:34:33.342
Come on! No, my kids!

00:34:33.349 --> 00:34:34.469
Sam's got your kids. Come on.

00:34:37.221 --> 00:34:38.315
Help!

00:34:38.972 --> 00:34:40.086
Please!

00:34:43.699 --> 00:34:44.813
Come here.

00:34:45.514 --> 00:34:47.106
Don't look, don't look.

00:35:00.454 --> 00:35:03.742
Sari, take your brother outside as
fast as you can and don't look back.

00:35:12.028 --> 00:35:13.617
Are you okay, baby?

00:35:13.640 --> 00:35:16.500
Sari, where's Sam? He's
inside. Something's got him.

00:35:38.772 --> 00:35:40.694
Ugh! Aah!

00:36:03.741 --> 00:36:04.319
Sam!

00:36:25.050 --> 00:36:25.881
Sam?!

00:36:26.782 --> 00:36:27.307
Sam!

00:36:32.062 --> 00:36:34.200
No, don't! Don't! What? Why?

00:36:35.513 --> 00:36:36.993
Because I know who it is.

00:36:37.769 --> 00:36:39.487
I can see her now.

00:36:56.613 --> 00:36:57.949
Mom.

00:37:08.264 --> 00:37:09.569
Dean.

00:37:24.916 --> 00:37:26.366
Sam.

00:37:32.844 --> 00:37:34.501
I'm sorry.

00:37:39.221 --> 00:37:40.883
F-For what?

00:37:53.190 --> 00:37:56.055
You, get out of my house.

00:37:56.872 --> 00:37:59.191
And let go of my son.

00:38:29.398 --> 00:38:30.970
Now it's over.

00:38:44.689 --> 00:38:45.943
Thanks for these.

00:38:46.455 --> 00:38:48.558
Don't thank me. They're yours.

00:38:53.269 --> 00:38:54.143
Well,

00:38:54.622 --> 00:38:58.218
There are no spirits in there
anymore, this time for sure.

00:38:59.402 --> 00:39:01.075
Not even my mom?

00:39:01.740 --> 00:39:03.075
No.

00:39:07.432 --> 00:39:08.921
What happened?

00:39:09.968 --> 00:39:14.625
Your mom's spirit and the poltergeists'
energy, they canceled each other out.

00:39:15.115 --> 00:39:18.704
Your mom destroyed herself
going after the thing.

00:39:19.961 --> 00:39:22.222
Why would she do something like that?

00:39:23.270 --> 00:39:26.349
Well, to protect her boys, of course.

00:39:34.224 --> 00:39:36.220
Sam, I'm sorry.

00:39:38.573 --> 00:39:39.963
For what?

00:39:40.493 --> 00:39:43.355
You sensed it was here, didn't you?

00:39:43.390 --> 00:39:45.115
Even when I couldn't.

00:39:50.123 --> 00:39:51.874
What's happening to me?

00:39:52.837 --> 00:39:55.839
I know I should have
all the answers, but...

00:39:57.540 --> 00:39:58.967
I don't know.

00:39:59.541 --> 00:40:00.984
Sam, you ready ?

00:40:06.044 --> 00:40:07.174
Bye.

00:40:10.167 --> 00:40:11.542
Bye Sam.

00:40:14.053 --> 00:40:15.213
Ah.

00:40:15.894 --> 00:40:18.235
Don't you boys be strangers.

00:40:18.658 --> 00:40:19.891
We won't.

00:40:21.438 --> 00:40:22.692
See you around.

00:40:53.999 --> 00:40:55.596
That boy...

00:40:57.228 --> 00:40:59.108
He has such

00:40:59.200 --> 00:41:01.195
Powerful abilities.

00:41:04.970 --> 00:41:07.707
Why he couldn't sense his own father,

00:41:07.919 --> 00:41:09.537
I have no idea.

00:41:15.289 --> 00:41:16.426
Mary's spirit...

00:41:18.219 --> 00:41:20.521
Do you really think she saved the boys?

00:41:22.860 --> 00:41:23.809
I do.

00:41:35.792 --> 00:41:38.515
John Winchester, I could just slap you.

00:41:38.581 --> 00:41:41.035
Why don't you go talk to your children?

00:41:42.667 --> 00:41:44.179
God, I want to.

00:41:46.164 --> 00:41:48.662
You have no idea how
much I want to see them.

00:41:51.602 --> 00:41:52.556
But I can't.

00:41:54.218 --> 00:41:54.923
Not yet.

00:42:01.463 --> 00:42:03.238
Not until I know the truth.



00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.000
